Commercial S3.2 phase-07 allowlist diagnosis
================================================

Observed at: 2026-08-29T15:48:26Z
Failed phase: 07_ALLOWLIST_LOAD

Safe symptom
------------

After the systemd credential-boundary correction, the transient startup probe
completed phases 01 through 06 and failed safely at phase 07. The main service
remained inactive, Restart remained no, NRestarts remained zero, and the
disabled contract plus consumed S3.1 authorization were restored exactly.

Proven root cause
-----------------

S3Allowlist.load_private had its own private-file predicate and still accepted
only the local 0600 representation. The systemd credential copy is root-owned,
mode 0440 and readable only through the service-user ACL. The separate
predicate rejected this safe runtime representation.

A network-free transient inspection proved that the allowlist content itself
is canonical and unchanged: exactly one binding, one CREATOR role and one
MODERATOR role. No Telegram IDs or creator identifiers were written to the
diagnostic evidence.

Correction boundary
-------------------

The allowlist loader keeps the local current-user-owned 0600 profile and adds
only the same root-owned /run/credentials systemd profile already enforced by
S3CredentialBoundary. Symlinks, alternate paths, alternate owners, broader
modes, multiple links, unreadable files, empty files and oversized files remain
rejected.

Rollback
--------

Restore application commit d7e78201f06ec493e7ecabcb4b624e5f92c9abf9
and its matching runtime verification authorization. This restores the proven
phase-07 failure without changing data or schema.
